Building TigerVNC with MSVC
===========================

MinGW is the supported toolchain on Windows. The headers in include/
provide the POSIX interfaces the sources expect and MSVC lacks, and are
only used when CMake detects MSVC.

Most dependencies can be installed with vcpkg:

  cmake -S . -B build -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A ARM64 \
    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=<vcpkg>/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake \
    -DVCPKG_TARGET_TRIPLET=arm64-windows

GnuTLS is not available in vcpkg for MSVC, so it has to be built
separately and specified manually:

  -DGNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIR=<gnutls>/include
  -DGNUTLS_LIBRARY=<gnutls>/lib/gnutls.lib
